Key Features Implemented:
User Management

Users table with roles (customer, admin, moderator)
Profile information, ratings, and wallet system

Book Management

Books table with detailed information (ISBN, title, description, etc.)
Authors and Publishers tables with relationships
Categories for genre-based organization
Book-Author and Book-Category many-to-many relationships

Marketplace Features

Book Listings: Users can sell, rent, or both
E-books: Digital book sales with download tracking
Stationery Items: Pencils, erasers, sharpeners, notebooks, etc.
Flexible pricing for different rental periods (daily, weekly, monthly)

Transaction System

Orders table supporting purchases, rentals, e-books, and stationery
Order items tracking with rental duration support
Multiple payment and shipping options

Review System

Book reviews with ratings (1-5 stars)
Helpfulness voting on reviews
Verified purchase tracking

Additional Features

Donations: Users can donate books to libraries/charities
Monthly Quizzes: Complete quiz system with questions, answers, and scoring
Wishlists: Users can save books they want
Shopping Cart: Temporary storage before purchase
Messaging: User-to-user communication
Notifications: System-wide notification system

Admin Features

Complete admin oversight with activity logging
Ability to manage all content (books, users, orders, donations, quizzes)
Admin logs for tracking all administrative actions

Performance Optimizations

Strategic indexes on frequently queried fields
Efficient data types and constraints
Normalized structure to avoid data redundancy

The schema supports advanced features like:

Multiple rental durations with flexible pricing
E-book download limits and DRM protection
Quiz ranking and scoring systems
Donation workflow with approval process
Comprehensive search and filtering capabilities


